  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "objective",
      "heading": "Research Information",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "The Aldarin Island is home to a diverse range of animals, the vast majority of which are herbivores. For years, these herbivores have thrived due to the minimal presence of predators and the Island's isolation causing it to be untouched by human development."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "However, [[coyote_intro]], a pack of Dashed Coyotes were introduced to the Island through unknown means. This has disrupted the ecological equilibrium of the Island, and the herbivore population has been declining year-by-year since."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Your team of ecologists have been assigned to study the population dynamics of various species on the Island."
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "Objective"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "[[objective_line]]"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "study",
      "heading": "Study Information",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "The four main prey for Dashed Coyotes were tracked and their population, split across the four areas of the Aldarin Island, are as follows:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "exhibit1",
      "heading": "Exhibit 1: Primary Prey Population Across Zones on Aldarin Island",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "table",
          "header": [
            "Zones",
            "Marmot",
            "Chinchilla",
            "Hare",
            "Gopher"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Teklan Hills",
